{"ukmt-tmc-2016-regional-crossnumber-01":[{"title":"Solution","body":"Start with the clues that stand alone.\n\n- 1A: $36$ is both triangular and square. 12A $=88^2+33^2=7744+1089=8833$; 3D $=12^2+33^2=144+1089=1233$; 14A $=2357$ (consecutive primes 2, 3, 5, 7); 23A $=3^3+4^3+5^3=216$; 18A $=22101$ (digit sum 6, crossing letters decide); 19D $=15$ (there are 15 primes below 50); 20D $=121$ ($121+4=125=5^3$); 25A $=\\sqrt{121}=11$; 16D $=1225=35^2=T_{49}$.\n- 5D $=36-2=34$. 22A $=216+121+15=352$. 2A is a two-digit factor of $352=2^5\\times11$ and the crossing gives $11$. 24A: $x+27=3x-79$ (11D is $27$, a cube), so $x=53$; 10A $=53+27=80$.\n- 4D $=1233+10\\times2357=24803$; 13D $=24803+8833=33636$.\n- 17A: the angles of an isosceles triangle with a $62^\\circ$ angle can be $62,62,56$ or $62,59,59$; the crossings give $56$.\n- 7A $=224$ and 1D $=336$, 6D $=63$ are factors of $2016=2^5\\cdot3^2\\cdot7$.\n- 8A $=66303=3\\times22101$ is a multiple of 18A. 4A $=243$ (multiple of 9). 9D $=648$ (digit sum 18). 12D $=85=81+4=49+36$. 15D $=500$ (column 8 has digits $4,0,5,0,0,1$, sum 10). 21D $=22=2\\times11$.\n\nEvery entry fits its clue and all crossings agree.\n\n**Answer:** Across: 1: 36; 2: 11; 4: 243; 7: 224; 8: 66303; 10: 80; 12: 8833; 14: 2357; 17: 56; 18: 22101; 22: 352; 23: 216; 24: 53; 25: 11.  Down: 1: 336; 3: 1233; 4: 24803; 5: 34; 6: 63; 9: 648; 11: 27; 12: 85; 13: 33636; 15: 500; 16: 1225; 19: 15; 20: 121; 21: 22."}]}